[Comment 4054380112 | 2026-03-13T11:17:59Z | https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime/issues/2649#issuecomment-4054380112]
How did you allocate the operations in qubits 3 and 5? How did you set the optimization level? 

[Comment 4054877280 | 2026-03-13T12:52:18Z | https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime/issues/2649#issuecomment-4054877280]
@sameermansoori2004 if you are interested in seeing the final schedule of pulses sent to the QPU, please consider turning `"scheduler_timing"` on, the documentation can be found here: https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/visualize-circuit-timing#enable-timing-data-retrieval

The number of CZ gates will be apparent. I am confident that there is no server-side transpilation that is reducing the number from what you have submitted. A fidelity revival could be attributed to coherent errors.

[Comment 4055319354 | 2026-03-13T14:04:44Z | https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-ibm-runtime/issues/2649#issuecomment-4055319354]
Hi Luciano,

 I manually selected qubits 3 and
5 because qubit 3 showed the cleanest calibration data (T1=275us, lowest
readout error).


